#
# The branch of 1bit-MONSTER/llama.cpp that mirrors AMD's HRX line, for the daily bump-hrx run
# (scripts/bump-hrx-sync.sh): the first line below that is not a comment. With no such line the mirror is
# `1bit/hrx-vulkan`, as it has always been.
#
# Why this is a file: no branch of the fork is ever force-moved (owner, 2026-11-10). When AMD rewrites its line
# so that its pin no longer descends from the mirror, AMD's new line is pushed to a NEW branch, named for the
# day, the old mirror is left exactly where it is, and that branch's name goes here. The workflow file is not
# edited. Order of work for such a move:
#   1. push AMD's pin to 1bit-MONSTER/llama.cpp as a new branch, e.g. 1bit/hrx-vulkan-20261110 (AMD's history
#      carries workflow files, so this push needs a token with `workflow` scope);
#   2. merge that branch into 1bit/hrx-vulkan-patched by an ordinary reviewed PR on the fork;
#   3. name the branch on a line below, and delete any commit line from config/llama-mirror-hold.config.
#
# No branch is named below, so the mirror is 1bit/hrx-vulkan.
